Task: codex-mark round 1 — Codex found P0 in my own fix; redesigned to out-of-band evidence
Action: The in-band `TRANSCRIPT COMPLETE` sentinel I added reproduced the exact bug it fixed, one layer up: reviewer stdout and the parent share the transcript, so a review that reads the diff or the docs QUOTES the sentinel — the review of that change emitted it 24 times. An incomplete run could quote both a stale verdict and the sentinel and be accepted as PASS. Replaced with an out-of-band `<log>.complete` sidecar recording the transcript's inode and byte length at completion; codex-mark requires it, verifies the inode still matches, and parses only those bytes. Sidecar is consumed with the log and cleared at run start so leftovers cannot vouch for a later run. A failed record write now returns exit 7 instead of reporting OK. Tests: nine cases across producer and consumer, including that a record quoted INTO the log does not count and that a verdict appended after completion is ignored.
